# Keep the overview current

When a change alters how someone runs, configures, or uses this project, update the matching doc in the same change. Skip docs for an internal refactor that does not change those facts.

- `README.md` — catalog counts and id pattern, features, config files, run and test commands.
- `src/cctv/README.md` — which package holds which code.
- `docs/AGENT.md` — tool loop, routing, config merge, HTTP API, config panel.
- `AGENTS.md` — how to run the API, UI, and tests, and which config file holds what.

```markdown
# BAD — new run command, README still shows the old one
make test

# GOOD — README Tests uses the command that actually runs
make test
```
